// frontend.jsonc: the browser client: its decisions, the copies it keeps, and the requirements its model is held to (an area part: items whose id starts fe-, d-fe- or copy-browser-).
// A part of the Strata specification; spec.jsonc lists the parts. Generated by scripts/split-spec.mjs
// the first time, edited in place after that. See specifications/README.md.
{
  "decisions": [
    {"id":"d-fe-1","ref":"D-FE-1","title":"The browser cache is a stamped copy, and correctness never depends on it (proposed)","group":"Frontend","source":"Proposed in docs/frontend.md (WG-5415); not yet decided by the owner.","statement":"**The browser cache is a stamped copy, and correctness never depends on it.** Every view result the web application keeps is stamped with the tenant epoch, the generation and the erasure epoch the gateway read it at, one stamp for the whole reply. It is drawn as current only while its stamp is the newest the browser has heard and its last contact is at most the contact bound old; a contact is the answer to a request the browser sent (a ping or a read), dated by the request's send time. An entry at the newest stamp whose contact is older is drawn as last checked, not fetched again; an older entry is drawn labelled with its age. View reads are issued with cache: 'no-store', and every answer echoes a nonce the request carried, so a replayed or cached answer is never taken as a contact. Stamps are compared only within a tenant epoch; with its tag the server sends the epoch's ordinal, set at every nonce rotation to the greater of the previous ordinal plus one and the rotation time in milliseconds, so it stays monotone across restores, re-creation and import. The browser switches epoch on a higher ordinal, or on any other tag in an answer, matched by its nonce, to a request sent after its last switch, whatever its ordinal; switching purges and resets its known stamp, floor and erasure epochs together; anything else of another tag is ignored. The browser re-reads the time before it draws after a page becomes visible or wakes. A missing or evicted entry is a read from the gateway, never an error, and every write is decided again by the server."},
    {"id":"d-fe-2","ref":"D-FE-2","title":"Three stores in the browser, each for one kind of content (proposed)","group":"Frontend","source":"Proposed in docs/frontend.md (WG-5415); not yet decided by the owner.","statement":"**Three stores in the browser, each for one kind of content.** A service worker keeps only content named by its hash (the built files, the fonts, the parts of the tenant's interface definition) in the Cache API and passes every other request through; the bootstrapped page, which carries the session, is never stored, and a navigation falls back to a stored shell after a timeout. IndexedDB holds view results, the write queue and drafts, encrypted per principal: each record persists the stamp it was read at, the partition persists, for the current tenant epoch, its known stamp, its floor and its erasure epochs, carry-forward happens in memory, and the encryption's additional data binds the record to its partition, store, key and erasure epoch only. Encryption runs outside any IndexedDB transaction; each write is then checked and made in one short transaction, against the partition's current key id and the record's version. The kernel worker's memory holds the hot set."},
    {"id":"d-fe-3","ref":"D-FE-3","title":"One leader tab per principal, chosen with Web Locks and kept by a heartbeat (proposed)","group":"Frontend","source":"Proposed in docs/frontend.md (WG-5415); not yet decided by the owner.","statement":"**One leader tab per principal, chosen with Web Locks and kept by a heartbeat.** Each tab keeps its own kernel worker. The worker holding the exclusive lock of the site and principal opens the socket, drains the write queue and writes a heartbeat to IndexedDB; a follower that sees the heartbeat stop takes the lock over with a stealing request. The others hear notices on a BroadcastChannel and read the shared IndexedDB. A SharedWorker is not used: Chrome for Android re-enabled it only in 2026 and Samsung Internet does not support it."},
    {"id":"d-fe-4","ref":"D-FE-4","title":"Custom elements draw, the kernel decides (proposed)","group":"Frontend","source":"Proposed in docs/frontend.md (WG-5415); not yet decided by the owner.","statement":"**Custom elements draw, the kernel decides.** Web Components are renderers of the view model: they hold no application state, take properties, and report what the person did as events the main thread turns into kernel messages. They render into the light DOM so that labels, ARIA references and the page's styles reach them; a control with no native element is form-associated through ElementInternals. Declarative Shadow DOM is not used, because nothing is rendered on the server and no markup is parsed (D18)."},
    {"id":"d-fe-5","ref":"D-FE-5","title":"Writes made offline are queued intents, decided again by the server (proposed)","group":"Frontend","source":"Proposed in docs/frontend.md (WG-5415); not yet decided by the owner.","statement":"**Writes made offline are queued intents, decided again by the server.** A queued write holds the intent, the tenant epoch and record version it was decided on (none for a create) and an idempotency key drawn, in one transaction with any rewrite of its input, once that input is final. A write that depends on another's result holds a random local id and no key until that result is known; the rewrite is computed outside a transaction and committed by compare-and-swap on the entry's version, and the write is decided again by the person when the result was learned only by a lookup or differs from what they saw. The time of a write's first sending is made durable before its first byte; a create with no durable first sending is never resent before the server is asked for the recorded outcome of its key, and that lookup fences the key: the server records a tombstone, kept for the key's idempotency retention, scoped to the tenant, principal and contract, and checked in the same store transaction as a commit, so the original request cannot commit afterwards; a resend then uses a new key. The server commits a write only at its stamp, or, for a contract whose policies follow references, at the tenant generation it was decided on. A conflict is never merged silently: the person decides."},
    {"id":"d-fe-6","ref":"D-FE-6","title":"What cannot be done offline (proposed)","group":"Frontend","source":"Proposed in docs/frontend.md (WG-5415); not yet decided by the owner.","statement":"**What cannot be done offline.** Only an operation whose contract allows queueing may be queued; by default none does. Sign-in, step-up and anything needing a fresh authentication (D-700), payments and plan changes, roles, members, invitations, sessions, passkeys and second factors, schema changes and the Impact Lab, and subject rights requests are never queued. Sign-out works offline: it deletes the browser's key, device id and device secret at once, and tells the gateway on the next connection."},
    {"id":"d-fe-7","ref":"D-FE-7","title":"Data at rest is encrypted under a key held per enrolled device (proposed)","group":"Frontend","source":"Proposed in docs/frontend.md (WG-5415); not yet decided by the owner.","statement":"**Data at rest is encrypted under a key held per enrolled device.** The identity service enrols a device for a principal, issues its device id and a device secret, and keeps a random key share and a hash of the secret, sealed at rest, for a fixed lifetime from enrolment with rotation before it ends. It gives the share only to a session of that principal that presents the secret; the device id is not a credential. Rotation keeps a current key id in the partition: every append and rewrite names the key id it encrypted under and is refused unless it is current, and re-encryption is a compare-and-swap on each record's version. The worker derives a non-extractable AES-GCM key from the share and keeps it in memory. This protects against the next user of the device and against a disk read after the key and secret are gone; it does not protect against code running in the origin while the person is signed in."},
    {"id":"d-fe-8","ref":"D-FE-8","title":"An erasure epoch per object type, read before opening (proposed)","group":"Frontend","source":"Proposed in docs/frontend.md (WG-5415); not yet decided by the owner.","statement":"**An erasure epoch per object type, read before opening.** The browser holds opened values, so a key destruction (D-350), which raises no generation, would leave them current. The server keeps a destruction log keyed by object type and sealed field and derives from it an erasure epoch per object type, with no audience class enumerated; a key destruction raises, in its transaction, the epoch of every type with a field sealed under the destroyed key. A reply carries the epoch of each type its view depends on, a frame and an answer to a ping those of the types the subscriber reads; a read takes them before, or atomically with, opening its sealed fields. Readers of a type learn that an erasure touched that type, not whose. On a new epoch the browser deletes every view result, every base value of a queued write and every value in a draft that came from the server, for that type, in the same transaction that raises its known epoch, and drops any later put of an older one; the cost is a refetch of those views."},
    {"id":"d-fe-9","ref":"D-FE-9","title":"No third-party code reaches the browser (proposed)","group":"Frontend","source":"Proposed in docs/frontend.md (WG-5415); not yet decided by the owner.","statement":"**No third-party code reaches the browser.** The QR code of an authenticator enrolment is drawn by an encoder of the web application's own, and the fonts are served from the site's own built files. Vite stays as the build tool; Playwright, axe and tsc stay as tools of development."},
    {"id":"d-fe-10","ref":"D-FE-10","title":"The kernel runs the interface scenarios without a browser (proposed)","group":"Frontend","source":"Proposed in docs/frontend.md (WG-5415); not yet decided by the owner.","statement":"**The kernel runs the interface scenarios without a browser.** A driver in Node runs the real kernel and the shell's view functions against the real gateway, interprets each uiScenario's steps against the drawn tree, and injects faults (lost replies, dropped sockets, reloads, a second tab) at the driver's boundary from a seed. Steps only a browser can answer run in Playwright."},
    {"id":"d-fe-11","ref":"D-FE-11","title":"Browser copies are reached at the next connection, within the realm's idle session lifetime","group":"Frontend","decided":"2026-11-22","owner":"owner","source":"Owner decision of 2026-11-22, recorded in WG-5415.","statement":"**Browser copies are reached at the next connection, within the realm's idle session lifetime.** Erasure, correction, restriction (PRV-352) and a reader's loss of permission reach a browser copy at the browser's next connection, and no later than the realm's idle session lifetime (twelve hours by default). Keeping data usable offline beyond a session is off by default and a realm opts in; a device that opted in is reached only when it next connects. A copy left on disk after a session ended without sign-out is consistent with this: its key is gone, so it cannot be read, while its device id and secret remain, so the same principal signing in again unlocks it, and the first answer's stamp and floor purge it before anything is drawn. PRV-351, PRV-352, PRV-353 and, as needed, CPY-013 and the permission-change requirements are amended to say this (WG-5449)."},
    {"id":"d-fe-12","ref":"D-FE-12","title":"Changes the server cannot notify (proposed)","group":"Frontend","source":"Proposed in docs/frontend.md (WG-5415); not yet decided by the owner.","statement":"**Changes the server cannot notify.** A notice names the keys that may differ since the previous frame on its connection. A view whose policies follow references names, in its depends_on, the object types those policies follow (AGG-042), and a commit to such a type sends the subscriber a frame naming those types without record ids, which discloses only that something changed in a type the subscriber's policies already read. A view whose policies read the clock, or whose query the kernel cannot resolve, is volatile: the server marks it by the classifier it already uses to refuse a shared copy (the aggregates classifier, less its principal condition, which does not apply to a copy kept for one principal), and every frame names it. Type-level frames are coalesced per connection within a window, so a hot type does not mean a frame per commit; every frame sent while a commit is deferred names the union of what is deferred over its whole interval. A restriction (PRV-352) sends a restriction notice; a membership, role, restriction or permission change raises the principal's access generation, and a change of a Read policy, or of the definition of a team or role a policy reads, raises the tenant's policy generation, one write for every principal (adding or removing a member of a team raises only that member's access generation); every answer carries the floor, the greater of the two, below which the browser keeps nothing; an out-of-commit change that alters what a principal may read sends a resync."},
    {"id":"d-fe-13","ref":"D-FE-13","title":"The person's own typed text survives a revocation or an erasure, for a while","group":"Frontend","decided":"2026-11-22","owner":"owner","source":"Owner decision of 2026-11-22, recorded in WG-5415.","statement":"**The person's own typed text survives a revocation or an erasure, for a while.** The person's own typed text survives the revocation or erasure that orphaned it, so they can copy it out with a 'copy and dismiss' action. The draft records that it is orphaned, with the time and the erasure epoch at orphaning of the object type of the record it edits; the typed text is deleted at the realm's idle session lifetime after orphaning, or by the next erasure after that (an erasure epoch newer than the one recorded), whichever comes first. Other people's data in the draft is removed at once."},
    {"id":"d-fe-14","ref":"D-FE-14","title":"Tenant scripts run in the browser, in a sandbox the browser kernel owns, and never on the server","group":"Frontend","decided":"2026-11-26","owner":"owner","source":"Owner decision of 2026-11-26, recorded in WG-5675.","statement":"**Tenant scripts run in the browser, in a sandbox the browser kernel owns, and never on the server.** A tenant script is a WebAssembly module; a JavaScript engine compiled to WebAssembly covers JavaScript. It runs in a dedicated worker inside a sandboxed iframe on a separate origin whose content security policy is default-src 'none'. It has no network, no timers, no DOM, no storage and no browser API. Its only imports are functions of the browser kernel: read the view data already shown to the person, redacted as the read rules require; return a UI tree of design-system components, which the kernel validates and renders; propose an intent, which the server decides with the person's own permissions; and keep a small state of its own. Each script has a memory cap, an instruction fuel budget enforced by instrumenting the module when it loads together with a hard timeout that terminates the worker, and an output size cap. The backend kernel never sees a script. Script output cannot inject markup, because the kernel draws the page from a closed vocabulary of DOM operations (WG-5677), and the platform's own interfaces still render from definitions (D-204)."}
  ],
  "copies": [
    {"id":"copy-browser-view","name":"Browser view result","of":["tbl-records"],"fields":["object","id","version","data"],"heldBy":"web-application","scope":"per-principal","freshness":{"bound":12,"unit":"hour","mechanism":"stamped with the tenant epoch, generation and erasure epoch of its reply; drawn as current only at the newest stamp heard and within the contact bound of the last pong; otherwise drawn labelled with its age; while offline, at most until the session would end unused, which a realm may shorten (IDN-259)","source":"d-fe-1"},"erasure":{"point":"the browser's next connection, and no later than the realm's idle session lifetime; a device whose realm opted in to keeping data usable offline beyond a session is reached only when it next connects","bound":12,"unit":"hour","source":"d-fe-11"},"dependsOnAuthority":true,"description":"View results kept in IndexedDB by the web application, per site and principal, encrypted under the key of the enrolled device (D-FE-7). Correctness never depends on it (D-FE-1)."},
    {"id":"copy-browser-queue","name":"Browser write queue","of":["tbl-records"],"fields":["object","id","version","data"],"heldBy":"web-application","scope":"per-principal","freshness":{"bound":7,"unit":"day","mechanism":"a queued intent with its key and decided stamp, removed when the gateway answers it; never resent past its key's retention less a margin (D-FE-5); values of other records are deleted on a new erasure epoch or a membership change (D-FE-8), and the person's own typed text is kept as D-FE-13 says","source":"d-fe-5"},"erasure":{"point":"the gateway's answer, sign-out on the device, or deletion of the device's share; erasure and correction reach it at the next connection and within the realm's idle session lifetime (D-FE-11)","bound":12,"unit":"hour","source":"d-fe-11"},"dependsOnAuthority":true,"description":"Writes the person made while offline, kept in IndexedDB encrypted under the key of the enrolled device until the leader tab has sent them and the gateway has answered, bounded in entries and bytes per principal."},
    {"id":"copy-browser-interface","name":"Browser interface definition","of":["tbl-schema-history"],"heldBy":"web-application","scope":"shared","freshness":{"bound":"zero","mechanism":"each part is named by the hash of its content, so a changed part is a new entry; the manifest is read again on every schema notice","source":"d-8250"},"erasure":{"point":"dropped when the manifest no longer lists it, or when the browser evicts the site's storage"},"description":"The parts of the tenant's interface definition, kept by the service worker in the Cache API. They hold no personal field and no record data (D-8250)."}
  ],
  "claims": [
    {"id":"fe-001","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the client cache model, in every schedule whose frames name every key touched in their interval, an answer returned as current SHALL be the server's opened value at the generation and erasure epoch the client last heard.","rationale":"Completeness of notices is the server's obligation; given it, a current answer is exactly what the server held at the stamp the client knows.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::current_value","lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::run_coh"],"ref":"FE-001","section":"The cache and its coherence","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Cache.read`","traces":["d-fe-1","d-fe-12","g-19","g-20"]},
    {"id":"fe-009","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the client cache model, a cached value that is not returned as current SHALL be returned labelled with the generation it was read at.","rationale":"Offline and while catching up, an older copy is still useful to read, as long as it says how old it is.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::read_stale_older"],"ref":"FE-009","section":"The cache and its coherence","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Cache.read`","traces":["d-fe-1","g-206"]},
    {"id":"fe-002","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the client cache model, a commit receipt read and sent at the server's current stamp, answering a request sent within the contact bound, SHALL make the next read of the written key return the committed value as current.","rationale":"A person who saves sees what they saved, not an older copy.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::read_after_commit","lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::receipt_read"],"ref":"FE-002","section":"The cache and its coherence","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Cache.put`","traces":["d-fe-1","g-206"]},
    {"id":"fe-003","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the client cache model, every generation and erasure epoch newer than the stamp of an answer returned as current SHALL have begun within the contact bound before the read.","rationale":"This bounds how far the stamp the browser knows lags the server, with no assumption on notices; it bounds no value, which needs complete notices.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::current_recent"],"ref":"FE-003","section":"The cache and its coherence","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Cache.read`","traces":["d-fe-1","g-19"]},
    {"id":"fe-012","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the client cache model, every entry at rest SHALL carry the erasure epoch the client has heard.","rationale":"A late reply or another tab's put of an older epoch must not write erased plaintext back after a purge.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::rest_one_epoch","lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::hear_purges"],"ref":"FE-012","section":"Privacy at rest","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Cache.put`","traces":["d-fe-8","d-350","g-350"]},
    {"id":"fe-004","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the client privacy model, a value kept at rest for one principal SHALL open with no key the browser holds for another principal.","rationale":"Separation on a shared device rests on which keys are present, not on which partition the code chooses to open.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Privacy.lean::no_cross_principal","lean/Strata/Client/Privacy.lean::served_own"],"ref":"FE-004","section":"Privacy at rest","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Privacy.Opens`","traces":["d-fe-7","g-20"]},
    {"id":"fe-005","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the client privacy model, after a principal signs out, with or without a connection, no value the principal left at rest SHALL open with any key the browser then or later holds, whatever device id a session of that principal names.","rationale":"Sign-out on a shared device must leave nothing readable, even when deleting the stored data did not complete or the gateway never heard of it, and even to a session of the same principal elsewhere.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Privacy.lean::signout_erases","lean/Strata/Client/Privacy.lean::offline_signout_erases"],"ref":"FE-005","section":"Privacy at rest","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Privacy.step` (signOut, signOutOffline, fetchById)","traces":["d-fe-6","d-fe-7","g-20"]},
    {"id":"fe-006","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the client privacy model, after a session ends, a value its principal left at rest SHALL open only after a session of that same principal fetches a key share again.","rationale":"Queued work survives an expired session for its own author and for no one else.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Privacy.lean::expire_locks","lean/Strata/Client/Privacy.lean::unlock_needs_own_session"],"ref":"FE-006","section":"Privacy at rest","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Privacy.step` (expire, fetchKey, fetchById)","traces":["d-fe-7","g-20","g-206"]},
    {"id":"fe-013","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the client rotation model, at every point of every schedule of rotation steps, appends and rewrites by other tabs under any key id, and crashes, every record SHALL be under a key whose share is still held.","rationale":"Rotating the device key must lose no data whenever it stops, and another tab may append at any point.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Privacy.lean::rot_no_loss","lean/Strata/Client/Privacy.lean::rot_no_lost_update","lean/Strata/Client/Privacy.lean::rot_finish_retires"],"ref":"FE-013","section":"Privacy at rest","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Privacy.rstep`","traces":["d-fe-7","g-206"]},
    {"id":"fe-007","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the offline write model, a first submission of a queued write SHALL commit only when the kernel allows it and, for a write with a stamp, the tenant is at the expected epoch and the record at the expected version.","rationale":"A write decided offline on an old copy must not overwrite a change it never saw, and a restore must not make an old version match.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Queue.lean::submit_ok_guard","lean/Strata/Client/Queue.lean::submit_classes"],"ref":"FE-007","section":"Offline writes","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Queue.Srv.submit`","traces":["d-fe-5","d-6595","g-206"]},
    {"id":"fe-010","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the offline write model, a submission of a queued write that does not commit SHALL leave every record, its version and its value unchanged.","rationale":"A conflict, a refusal and a repeated key are reported to the person and change nothing.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Queue.lean::submit_not_ok_unchanged"],"ref":"FE-010","section":"Offline writes","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Queue.Srv.submit`","traces":["d-fe-5","g-206"]},
    {"id":"fe-008","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the offline write model, in every schedule in which the server keeps each committed key for the retention and the client sends each key only within the retention of first sending it, a queued write SHALL be applied at most once.","rationale":"Reloads, lost replies and a second tab resend queued writes; each must take effect once, which rests on two local rules, one for each side.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Queue.lean::at_most_once"],"ref":"FE-008","section":"Offline writes","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Queue.run`","traces":["d-fe-5","d-fe-3","d-6595","g-206"]},
    {"id":"fe-011","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the offline write model, a queued write carrying the tenant epoch and the record version SHALL be applied at most once, whatever keys the server forgets and whatever restores occur.","rationale":"An update or delete decided on an epoch and version cannot apply twice, because its first application moves the record off that stamp for good and a restore moves the tenant to a new epoch.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Queue.lean::stamped_at_most_once"],"ref":"FE-011","section":"Offline writes","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Queue.run`","traces":["d-fe-5","d-6595","g-206"]},
    {"id":"fe-015","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the client cache model, no entry read below the floor the client has heard, the greater of the principal's access generation and the tenant's policy generation, SHALL be kept at rest.","rationale":"A late reply read before a revocation must not write revoked data back after the purge.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::rest_above_floor","lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::hear_access_purges","lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::contact_floor"],"ref":"FE-015","section":"Privacy at rest","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Cache.put`","traces":["d-fe-11","d-fe-12","g-20"]},
    {"id":"fe-016","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the lookup fence model, a key that a lookup found not committed SHALL never be committed afterwards.","rationale":"After a not-found lookup the client resends a create under a new key; the original request still in flight must not commit as well.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Queue.lean::fence_holds"],"ref":"FE-016","section":"Offline writes","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Queue.fstep`","traces":["d-fe-5","g-206"]},
    {"id":"fe-017","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the draft model, the person's own typed text in an orphaned draft SHALL be deleted at the idle session lifetime after orphaning or at the next erasure after it, whichever comes first.","rationale":"The owner's decision D-FE-13: the text survives the change that orphaned it, for the person to copy out, and no longer.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Drafts.lean::gone_after_next_erasure","lean/Strata/Client/Drafts.lean::gone_after_idle","lean/Strata/Client/Drafts.lean::survives_orphaning_erasure","lean/Strata/Client/Drafts.lean::orphan_drops_server_values"],"ref":"FE-017","section":"Privacy at rest","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Drafts.dstep`","traces":["d-fe-13","g-206","g-350"]},
    {"id":"fe-018","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the client cache model, no entry from a tenant epoch other than the current one SHALL be kept at rest.","rationale":"A restore or a re-created tenant restarts its counter; comparing its stamps with the old epoch's would drop everything, and keeping the old epoch's entries would mix two tenants' states.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::rest_same_tenant_epoch","lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::tenant_epoch_purges","lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::older_epoch_ignored"],"ref":"FE-018","section":"The cache and its coherence","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Cache.epochOf`","traces":["d-fe-1","g-20"]},
    {"id":"fe-019","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the client cache model, an answer sent in the server's current tenant epoch SHALL bring the client to that epoch, whatever answers of other epochs arrived before.","rationale":"Rotations are routine (every lease acquisition draws a new nonce) and answers arrive out of order; the client must not be left stuck in an older epoch.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::contact_reaches_current_epoch","lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::out_of_order_epochs_recover","lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::later_request_is_authoritative","lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::lower_ordinal_recovers"],"ref":"FE-019","section":"The cache and its coherence","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Cache.epochOf`","traces":["d-fe-1","g-19"]},
    {"id":"fe-014","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the client queue model, every submission of one idempotency key SHALL carry the same input.","rationale":"Keys are drawn once a write's input is final, in the same transaction as any rewrite of a local id, so the at-most-once results apply to the writes the client actually sends.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Queue.lean::q2_sent"],"ref":"FE-014","section":"Offline writes","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Queue.cstep`","traces":["d-fe-5","g-206"]},
    {"id":"fe-020","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"A tenant script running in the browser sandbox SHALL have only the browser kernel's own functions as its imports, so that it reaches no cookie, web storage, session token, network address, timer or element of the page DOM.","rationale":"D-FE-14: a tenant script is untrusted code, so the browser state that carries the person's session and the platform's network are out of its reach.","ref":"FE-020","section":"Tenant scripts in the browser sandbox","boundaryDetail":"the import table the browser kernel gives a tenant script","traces":["d-fe-14","k-4","k-6","k-16"]},
    {"id":"fe-021","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"A tenant script that exceeds its instruction fuel, its memory cap, its output size cap or its hard timeout SHALL be stopped, with the page still working.","rationale":"A script that loops or grows without bound must cost its own sandbox and nothing else on the page.","ref":"FE-021","section":"Tenant scripts in the browser sandbox","boundaryDetail":"the fuel, memory, output and timeout limits of the sandbox worker","traces":["d-fe-14","g-4"]},
    {"id":"fe-022","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"A tenant script SHALL receive only the view data that the person may read, after the read rules have redacted it.","rationale":"The script sees what the person sees and no more, so the sandbox adds no read that the page did not already allow.","ref":"FE-022","section":"Tenant scripts in the browser sandbox","boundaryDetail":"the read function the browser kernel gives a tenant script","traces":["d-fe-14","g-20"]},
    {"id":"fe-023","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"An intent that a tenant script proposes SHALL be decided by the server with the person's own permissions before it has any effect.","rationale":"A script acts only as the person it runs for, through the same decision a person's own action takes.","ref":"FE-023","section":"Tenant scripts in the browser sandbox","boundaryDetail":"the intent function the browser kernel gives a tenant script, and the server's decision on it","traces":["d-fe-14","k-13","d-506"]},
    {"id":"fe-024","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"The DOM operations that the browser kernel emits for any tenant script output SHALL create no script-capable element (script, iframe, object, embed, base, link or meta).","rationale":"Script output becomes page content only through the closed DOM vocabulary of WG-5677, so no output can carry script into the page.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Dom.lean::script_output_emits_no_script_element"],"ref":"FE-024","section":"Tenant scripts in the browser sandbox","boundaryDetail":"the DOM operations the browser kernel emits for a tenant script's UI tree","traces":["d-fe-14","k-12","d-204"]},
    {"id":"fe-025","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"The DOM operations that the browser kernel emits for any tenant script output SHALL set no event-handler, style, srcdoc or formaction attribute.","rationale":"Script output becomes page content only through the closed DOM vocabulary of WG-5677, so no output can carry script into the page.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Dom.lean::script_output_sets_no_handler_style_or_url"],"ref":"FE-025","section":"Tenant scripts in the browser sandbox","boundaryDetail":"the DOM operations the browser kernel emits for a tenant script's UI tree","traces":["d-fe-14","k-12","d-204"]},
    {"id":"fe-026","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"The DOM operations that the browser kernel emits for any tenant script output SHALL set href or src only to a URL that the trusted-URL policy accepts.","rationale":"Script output becomes page content only through the closed DOM vocabulary of WG-5677, so no output can carry script into the page.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Dom.lean::script_output_sets_no_handler_style_or_url"],"ref":"FE-026","section":"Tenant scripts in the browser sandbox","boundaryDetail":"the DOM operations the browser kernel emits for a tenant script's UI tree","traces":["d-fe-14","k-12","d-204"]}
  ]
}
